item.content:encoded:
VR isn't slowing down, and the numbers from 2026 show it 💸
In our latest blog post, @c_pruett, Director of Games at Meta, shares how we're investing in VR and where the ecosystem stands heading into 2027 👉 https://developers.meta.com/vr/blog/what-to-expect-meta-vr-ecosystem-holiday-season-2027/?utm_source=social-x&utm_medium=MVRD&utm_campaign=organic&utm_content=VREcosystem
Highlights 👇 (1/4) https://x.com/MetaVRDevs/status/2120223311716364719/photo/1
@c_pruett 💰 Money trends from 2026 so far:
👉 From January to September 2026, each of the top 50 apps made over $1M in revenue after store fees. 👉 IAP passed premium app sales as the Meta Store's largest revenue source for the first time. 👉 12 major new hits launched in 12 months (2/4)
@c_pruett 💡 Chris Pruett's advice for studios:
Pick one audience and design for it early, because that choice drives everything else. If you're building with Meta VR Glasses in mind, treat hand tracking as its own input mechanism from day 1, not a port of your controller scheme. (3/4)
@c_pruett 💫 One last takeaway:
The holiday spike and the Meta VR Glasses launch will bring a lot of new people into the ecosystem over the next 12 months. The audience is already more diverse than ever, so decide who you're building for now.
Read the full post 👉
